# sAIfe runs on your own API keys. Copy this file to .env and fill in what you use:
#     Copy-Item .env.example .env      (PowerShell)   or   cp .env.example .env
# .env is gitignored: never commit it. sAIfe reads keys only from the environment,
# redacts them from logs, and never writes them to traces or reports.
# Check what sAIfe will use (keys are never printed):  uv run python -m saife config

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Verifier: REQUIRED. Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
#    It runs the judges, and with the default routing every other role too.
#    Default: Google's own Gemini endpoint. Free key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SAIFE_VERIFIER_API_KEY=
SAIFE_VERIFIER_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
SAIFE_VERIFIER_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# Other endpoints work the same way, for example:
#   OpenRouter:  SAIFE_VERIFIER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#                SAIFE_VERIFIER_MODEL=google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite
#   Any other OpenAI-compatible gateway: its base URL and model ID.
# Claims and source excerpts are sent to this endpoint. For sensitive data, prefer the
# model provider's own endpoint over a third-party gateway.
# After setting or changing the endpoint, run once:
#     uv run python scripts/probe_verifier.py
# It checks the key and picks the structured-output mode the endpoint really enforces.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Second provider: OPTIONAL, recommended. Keeps checks independent (PRD P3).
#    With only a verifier key, `saife run` has Gemini write the answers that Gemini then
#    judges. Routing the generator to a different lab's model fixes that.
#    Key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
#    Free models (":free") allow 50 requests a day and 20 a minute until $10 of credit
#    has been bought (then 1,000 a day). Paid models need credit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# SAIFE_ROLE_GENERATE=openrouter:nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Per-role overrides: OPTIONAL. SAIFE_ROLE_<ROLE>=provider:model
#    provider: verifier | openrouter | anthropic
#    roles:    GENERATE, DECOMPOSE, REPAIR, GROUNDING_JUDGE, CONSISTENCY_JUDGE,
#              WEB_JUDGE, WEB_RETRIEVAL
#    Example with paid OpenRouter credit (Claude writes, splits and repairs):
# SAIFE_ROLE_GENERATE=openrouter:anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5
# SAIFE_ROLE_DECOMPOSE=openrouter:anthropic/claude-opus-5
# SAIFE_ROLE_REPAIR=openrouter:anthropic/claude-opus-5
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Anthropic: OPTIONAL. Needed only for the strict preset's web evidence (Claude web
#    search) or for the original Claude + verifier routing. Key: https://console.anthropic.com
#    Without it, strict's web checks come back UNVERIFIABLE (never silently skipped).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAIFE_ROUTING=split
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. sAIfe Monitor dashboard: OPTIONAL. Your own deployment of dashboard/ on Vercel's
#    free tier (see dashboard/README.md). When both are set, every run's events go to it
#    (HMAC-signed), and `saife bench` publishes its summary there.
#    The secret must match SAIFE_DASHBOARD_SECRET on Vercel; use 16+ random characters.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAIFE_DASHBOARD_URL=https://<your-project>.vercel.app
# SAIFE_DASHBOARD_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Advanced
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Force a structured-output mode instead of the probe result: json_schema | json_object | text
# SAIFE_VERIFIER_STRUCTURED_MODE=
# Verifier price in USD per million tokens, so reports show a real cost estimate
# (Claude prices are built in; OpenRouter free models cost 0):
# SAIFE_VERIFIER_PRICE_IN=
# SAIFE_VERIFIER_PRICE_OUT=
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
